  "summary_en": "Brazil's national AI strategy (EBIA) from the Ministry of Science, Technology and Innovation. Built on OECD principles, it sets nine thematic axes (regulation and ethics, governance, international aspects, education, workforce, R&D, productive sectors, public sector, public security) and favours cautious, principle-based regulation, sandboxes and innovation over new binding rules.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Grounded in the five OECD AI principles; nine thematic axes with strategic actions",
   "Avoids premature AI-specific regulation; prefers principle-based, outcome-based, context-sensitive approaches",
   "Calls for human intervention parameters for high-risk automated decisions and for algorithmic bias mitigation",
   "Promotes regulatory sandboxes, impact reports (data protection, security, human rights) and an AI observatory",
   "Calls for a data protection law for public security uses and oversight of AI surveillance"
